# Atelier demo-github environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in the values
# below before running the demo. Atelier's thesis is **dynamic UI**: routes
# are LLM-compiled from a recipe + intent + the catalog. A demo without
# a Gemini key falls back to hand-written manifests, which is fine for
# offline iteration but is NOT representative of how Atelier is meant to
# render in production. See `docs/ethos.md` principle #1.
#
# ─── Compiler (REQUIRED for the showcase experience) ────────────────────
# Get a key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. The pipeline is:
#   GeminiCompiler (cold = gemini-2.5-pro, diff = gemini-2.5-flash)
#     → cascade to FallbackCompiler (hand-written manifests in lib/) on
#       network blip / output validation failure / rate-limit.
#
# Without a key, every route renders via the FallbackCompiler. Token
# counter stays at 0; cache hits are vacuous; lens-switch produces the
# same hand-written output. The framework's dynamic-UI thesis is NOT
# being demonstrated.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Override the model ids if you want to point at a different version.
# GEMINI_COLD_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
# GEMINI_DIFF_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ─── Vault ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAULT_URL=http://localhost:4001
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAULT_FALLBACK=allow

# ─── App identity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_APP_ID=cir.demo-github
